{"name":"Castaway Beach","hex":"#d0c19f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"castaway","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cast adrift or ashore; marooned.","Shipwrecked."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shipwrecked sailor.","A discarded person or thing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/castaway"},{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Castaway","blocks":[{"text":"A castaway is a person who is cast adrift or ashore. While the situation usually happens after a shipwreck, some people voluntarily stay behind on a desert island, either to evade captors or the world in general. A person may also be left ashore as punishment (marooned)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Rescue_by_seamen_of_USNS_Passumpsic.jpg/330px-Rescue_by_seamen_of_USNS_Passumpsic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castaway","wikidata":"Q508230"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https: